+# Xcode plist XML decode
+
+Reverified the premise before editing: `rg -n 'groob/plist|com_github_groob_plist' --glob '!go.sum' --glob '!MODULE.bazel.lock'` found exactly one Go import and one BUILD dependency, both in server/xcode, plus shared dependency declarations. The actual file read is `Contents/version.plist`; the existing implementation already uses an XML-only decoder. The dependency reduction is real; binary size was not measured.
+
+Replaced groob/plist with encoding/xml in platform-neutral xcode_plist.go. The parser reads ordered key/value elements, keeps the two version strings, and skips entire unknown values (including nested dictionaries and arrays). Existing file-open/decode error wrappers remain; the opened file is now closed. Tests exercise a fixture with reordered keys, unknown nested values, missing fields, malformed pairs, wrong field types, missing root dictionaries, and truncated XML. Added the parser and its Linux-runnable test to BUILD.
+
+## Measurements
+
+Same measurement code for HEAD (before) and the working tree (after), counting server/xcode Go files and BUILD only:
+
+| Metric | Before | After |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| go_library/go_test targets | 2 | 2 |
+| Unique direct dependency labels | 6 | 5 |
+| Unique external dependency labels | 2 | 1 |
+| Lines of Go and BUILD | 434 | 565 |
+| First-party groob/plist imports | 1 | 0 |
+
+Reused the existing xcode_test target and removed its macOS compatibility restriction so the portable tests run on Linux. The locator tests remain Darwin-only via their source build tag. Dependency counts include both existing targets and all platform-select branches, excluding platform selector labels.
+
+Measurement command (run before committing; HEAD is the baseline):
+
+```sh
+python3 - <<'PY'
+import pathlib,re,subprocess
+for label in ['before','after']:
+ if label=='before':
+  paths=subprocess.check_output(['git','ls-tree','-r','--name-only','HEAD','server/xcode'],text=True).splitlines()
+  texts={p:subprocess.check_output(['git','show','HEAD:'+p],text=True) for p in paths if p.endswith('.go') or p.endswith('/BUILD')}
+ else: texts={str(p):p.read_text() for p in pathlib.Path('server/xcode').iterdir() if p.suffix=='.go' or p.name=='BUILD'}
+ build=texts['server/xcode/BUILD']
+ deps=set()
+ for block in re.findall(r'    deps = select\(\{(.*?)\n    \}\),',build,re.S): deps.update(re.findall(r'^\s+"((?:@|//)[^"]+)",$',block,re.M))
+ print(label, len(re.findall(r'^go_(?:library|test)\(',build,re.M)),len(deps),sum(d.startswith('@') for d in deps),sum(len(s.splitlines()) for s in texts.values()))
+PY
+```
+
+## Verification
+
+- `go test ./server/xcode/...`: PASS on Linux.
+- `go test server/xcode/xcode_plist.go server/xcode/xcode_plist_test.go`: PASS.
+- `GOOS=darwin go vet ./server/xcode/...`: FAIL: existing xcode_darwin_test.go references NewXcodeLocator, but cross-compilation disables cgo and excludes xcode_darwin.go. Apple CoreServices requires a Darwin SDK/toolchain.
+- `GOOS=darwin go vet server/xcode/xcode_plist.go server/xcode/xcode_plist_test.go`: PASS.
+- `GOOS=darwin go test -c -o /tmp/xcode-plist-darwin.test server/xcode/xcode_plist.go server/xcode/xcode_plist_test.go`: PASS (Darwin cross-compile of parser and tests).
+- `git diff --check`: PASS.
+
+- `bazel test //server/xcode:xcode_test`: PASS on Linux, including nogo checks. Final log: /tmp/xcode-bazel-test-complete.log. An initial separate parser-test target also passed; it was subsequently consolidated into xcode_test to keep the target count unchanged.
+- `bazel build --config=target-darwin-arm64 //server/xcode:xcode`: PASS, including nogo checks. Final log: /tmp/xcode-darwin-build-complete.log. `go tool nm bazel-bin/server/xcode/xcode.a` confirms the archive contains NewXcodeLocator, xcodePlistForPath, and decodeXcodePlist, so the actual cgo Darwin locator was compiled.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //server/xcode:xcode, 1)'`: FAIL in unrelated Docker repository setup: default_execution_image Docker build timed out. Log: /tmp/xcode-rdeps-before.log.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(set(//server/xcode:all //enterprise/server/cmd/executor:all //enterprise/server/test/integration/remote_execution/rbetest:all), //server/xcode:xcode, 1)'`: FAIL during default_execution_image setup with disk exhaustion (exit 7). Log: /tmp/xcode-rdeps-scoped.log.
+- `rg -n '//server/xcode|server/xcode"' --glob BUILD --glob '*.go' enterprise server`: identifies executor_lib and rbetest as the direct consumers.
+- `bazel build //enterprise/server/cmd/executor:executor_lib //enterprise/server/test/integration/remote_execution/rbetest:rbetest`: FAIL after about 52 minutes, at GoCompilePkg //proto:failure_details_go_proto with compiler exit 1. The filesystem had only 2.4 MB free at failure; the compiler emitted no further diagnostic. These consumers are not fully verified. Log: /tmp/xcode-rdeps-build.log.
+
+Long Bazel commands ran under nohup with logs in /tmp and were polled to completion. Earlier Darwin and test attempts failed explicitly with "No space left on device"; final package test and Darwin build succeeded after cache cleanup. No native Darwin runtime tests could run on this Linux VM.
+
+## Dependency cleanup and scope
+
+`rg -n 'groob/plist|com_github_groob_plist' --glob '*.go' --glob BUILD --glob BUILD.bazel .` now returns no matches. github.com/groob/plist has no remaining first-party source or BUILD users. Its go.mod/go.sum and Bazel module declarations are intentionally left for the serialized dependency cleanup PR. No binary-size claim is made. All repository edits, including this report, are under server/xcode. To recover from the 25 GB filesystem filling during verification, removed unused Docker build cache (`docker builder prune -f`), disposable downloaded Bazel archive payloads (2.4 GB), Go's build cache (`go clean -cache`), and generated .a files in three configurations used by the failed consumer build. Extracted repositories and the package's compiled artifacts were retained. These cache operations were outside the source-edit scope and were necessary for the final verification; they changed no additional repository files. The large consumer build was not retried after disk exhaustion.
